{
  "id": "80669",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Calculating Free Energy",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Free energy is a state function, so its value depends only on the state of the system and not on how the system arrived at that state. For this reason, when a system undergoes a physical or chemical change, we can determine its "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "standard free energy change (Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "G"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ")"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "The change in free energy when one set of substances  is converted into another set of substances, with all substances in their standard states (1 bar pressure for gases, 1 M concentration for solutions)."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2323899213",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1892284634",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " solely from thermodynamic information about its initial and final states. We can calculate the standard free energy change for a process at a given temperature from its standard enthalpy and entropy changes using:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "1ebtk85gs71t6tu",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "obfi37k6y0enjyq",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "fkkekyw7ny6y3ei",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm\\Delta G^\\circ\\;=\\;\\mathrm\\Delta H^\\circ\\;-\\;T\\mathrm\\Delta S^\\circ",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "In some cases, we may know, or be given, the values of Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "H"
              },
              {
                "text": "° and Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "S"
              },
              {
                "text": "°. If these values are not available, we can calculate them from standard enthalpies of formation, Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "f"
              },
              {
                "text": "°, and standard entropies, "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "S"
              },
              {
                "text": "°, of the reactants and products. These values are found in the table of "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Standard Thermodynamic Properties for Selected Substances"
                  }
                ],
                "href": "https://cnx.org/contents/havxkyvS@9.525:2gdkQpYU@6/Standard-Thermodynamic-Propert",
                "linkType": "url",
                "target": "new",
                "type": "a"
              },
              {
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "km1lk2x9x711vew",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "1301777844",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
