        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "One step in the formation of acid rain is the oxidation of sulfur dioxide to sulfur trioxide:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "u2f3gyz6r6jyipl",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "uqnnta45kfk0tbp",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "cwa1is2bmw6gcra",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "2\\;{\\mathrm{SO}}_2(g)\\:+\\:{\\mathrm O}_2(g)\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;2\\;{\\mathrm{SO}}_3(g)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Determine the standard free energy change for this reaction at 25 °C, given that Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "H"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "° = −197.8 kJ and Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "S"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "° = −188.0 J/K. What does this value tell us about the spontaneity of this reaction?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1g3mqvo5sm82tjy",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We use the standard enthalpy and entropy changes to calculate the standard free energy change:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "07hbtc7y78ozqbx",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "usx8sgtnssbtgwa",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "hgvnf5ja14ty82g",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm\\Delta G^\\circ\\;=\\;\\mathrm\\Delta H^\\circ\\;-\\;T\\mathrm\\Delta S^\\circ",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "kajx2hbngmu7zlx",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "mvl5a23ncmqcp05",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "=\\;-197.8\\;\\mathrm{kJ}\\;-\\;(298.2\\;\\mathrm K)\\left(-188.0\\;\\frac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm K}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1\\; \\mathrm{kJ}}{1000\\;\\mathrm J}\\right)\\;=\\;-141.7\\;\\mathrm{kJ}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "G"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "° is negative, so the reaction is spontaneous at this temperature."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "fk28rfr21vc3y77",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "3542953155",
            "selection": {
              "anchor": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  0,
                  0
                ]
              },
              "focus": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  1,
                  0
                ]
              }
            },
            "type": "content"
          }
        ],
        "id": "808935803",
