      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "We can also calculate the standard free energy change (Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "G"
              },
              {
                "text": "°), for a given process from the "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "standard free energies of formation, Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "G"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "°"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "f"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Change in free energy accompanying the formation of one mole of substance from its elements in their standard states."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2331022781",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "4051219990",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": ", for the reactants and products. The standard free energy of formation is the free energy change that accompanies the formation of one mole of a substance from its elements in their standard states. Similar to the standard enthalpies of formation, Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "G"
              },
              {
                "text": "°"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "f"
              },
              {
                "text": " is by definition zero for elemental substances under standard state conditions. The approach to calculating the free energy change for a reaction is the same as that done previously for enthalpy and entropy changes. Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "G"
              },
              {
                "text": "°"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "f"
              },
              {
                "text": " values also available at "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Standard Thermodynamic Properties for Selected Substances"
                  }
                ],
                "href": "https://cnx.org/contents/havxkyvS@9.525:2gdkQpYU@6/Standard-Thermodynamic-Propert",
